<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Habib Bourguiba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1903–2000</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Habib Bourguiba was the leader of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>'s independence movement and the country's first president, from 1957 to 1987. A lawyer trained in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-destour">Neo-Destour</a> party in 1934, was repeatedly imprisoned by the French and negotiated independence in 1956, becoming prime minister and then president after the monarchy was abolished. He promoted secular education and women's rights but ruled a one-party state until deposed by Zine El Abidine Ben Ali.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/habib-bourguiba.jpg" alt="Habib Bourguiba" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Habib Osman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Habib_Bourguiba_portrait4_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
